OpenMCAD — LICENCE NOT YET DETERMINED
=====================================

No licence has been chosen for this project yet. This file is a deliberate placeholder,
not an oversight.

Until a licence is committed here, no permission to use, copy, modify, or distribute this
software is granted. Absence of a licence means all rights reserved by default; do not
assume otherwise.

WHY THIS IS OPEN
----------------

The plan this project is built from (docs/PLAN.md) points in two directions at once. The
name says open source. Section 17 of the plan schedules licensing and activation work
(node-locked and floating licences, trial mode, offline activation), which is proprietary
product work. Both are legitimate products. They are not the same product, and the choice
belongs to the project owner.

The options and the constraint each one places on the dependencies are set out in:

    docs/adr/0017-project-name-and-licence.md

WHAT IS ALREADY TRUE
--------------------

The architecture does not foreclose any option. The geometry kernel (OCCT) and the
constraint solver (planegcs) are both LGPL-2.1 (OCCT with the Open CASCADE Exception), and
both are confined to separately replaceable dynamic libraries by design -- see ADR-0003 and
ADR-0006. That was decided for engineering reasons and happens to keep every licensing door
open.

BEFORE FIRST PUBLIC RELEASE
---------------------------

Section 8.6 of the plan requires legal review of the licence posture before first public
release, not after. That instruction stands.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. Third-party components carry their own licences, which apply
regardless of what is eventually chosen for this project.
